# LiNC's copy of baiermill_pb/hallib/szgh_panel.hal, used by
# configs/baiermill-pb.ini. The machine tree is never edited.
#
# The machine's file starts the compiled helper:
#   loadusr ./szgh-panel-hal -c 0.01
# That binary is not in the machine tree. Its python driver is
# (baiermill_pb/szgh_panel_hal.py: executable, "#!/usr/bin/env python3",
# LinuxCNC's hal module + pyserial, no display), and the machine's own HAL file
# keeps that form as its first-line comment:
#   # loadusr ./szgh_panel_hal.py -c 0.01
# This file loads the python driver instead. The component name it creates is
# "szgh_panel" - the same pins the machine's post-GUI HAL nets - and "-c 0.01"
# is the machine's 10 ms panel cycle, so behaviour matches the intended entry.
#
# LinuxCNC changes to the INI's directory (configs/) before loading HAL, so this
# relative path resolves to ../baiermill_pb/szgh_panel_hal.py.
loadusr ../../baiermill_pb/szgh_panel_hal.py -c 0.01
